WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.380
Speaker 1: All right, let's get into this
week's mailbag info at David Pakman dot com

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.660
is the place to email if you have something
to say.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:13.169
Sometimes we'll take a YouTube comment or
a tweet reply or a Facebook message or whatever.

00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:18.970
Starting today, in fact, indeed, with a Facebook
message from Jionni who said, you look like

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.240
a SoI jack in real life effing loser.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.970
Now, this was a new one.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.810
I recently asked on my Twitter, What does
it mean to be compelled?

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.210
Not a term I had heard before last week, and
it was unclear what it meant.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.960
I also didn't know what a soy jack is, so
I look this one up.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:42.880
This one apparently is a meme which is often
used in online discourse where you post a

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.829
soy jack, which I guess is an image.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:50.770
And the idea is when you post it, you're saying
the person you're arguing online with is a

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.170
beta soy boy.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.170
So that's that.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.660
And apparently I am a soy jack in real life,
maybe not on the Internet, but in real life

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:00.660
I am a soy jack.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.180
So very, very important messaging there.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.850
Brandon wrote in about a potential Biden pardon
of Trump.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:13.100
And Brandon says David, longtime listener,
first time question, wondering if you could

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:18.880
unpack the hypothetical scenario of Biden
pardoning Trump in an effort to bring the

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:24.830
country together to avoid the inevitable political
and cultural turmoil of such a process?

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.020
Thank you for your levelheaded perspective.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.370
You know, I don't think it's completely out
of the realm of possibility that if the next

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:36.340
few months or the next year for Trump go in
a particular way, and I would call it going

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.549
south, for lack of a better term.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:45.799
I actually don't think it's completely impossible
that Biden would consider such a pardon again

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:50.680
to unite the country sort of in the way that
it happened with Nixon.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.040
But my hope is that he wouldn't do that, because
at some point we have to be if no one is above

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:01.880
the law, it means not only that anybody can
be charged, but it has to mean that people

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.310
actually have to have consequences for the
things that they do if they are found guilty

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.570
of doing those things.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:13.380
So I do think Brandon's instinct is right
that Biden does seem like the type of guy

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:20.610
who would go above partizanship and in certain
scenarios might say, I'm going to pardon Donald

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.610
Trump.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.910
We're thinking many steps ahead, but I hope
that it doesn't happen because I do think

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:31.160
that we really need to put our money where
our mouths are when it comes to individuals

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.980
not being above the law.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.800
And that means when there's a consequence,
you don't get out of it because you used to

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.150
be the president.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.800
Greg wrote in about this deep state assassination
plot theory.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:50.110
We've heard from right wingers like Steve
Bannon and Rudy Giuliani and others over the

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:55.630
