00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.960
And I think Jessica is completely correct.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:45.410
Paul wrote in about electric cars.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:53.680
And he does not like my recent defenses of
electric cars, saying cars are the most dangerous,

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:59.010
inefficient, expensive and environmentally
and socially harmful means of transportation

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:04.720
available electric cars reduce one of those
problems carbon emissions, although with some

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:10.120
offsetting costs in terms of mining, if you
really want to address the climate disaster,

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:14.290
you need to focus on a host of reforms which
will reduce or eliminate our dependency on

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.630
cars as our primary means of transportation.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.570
Listen, I'm right there with you.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.370
There is no greater advocate than me for better
public transit.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.550
This means both within and between cities.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:30.070
Our national rail is a complete and total
joke.

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:32.420
We are in many cities.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:33.940
Public transit is a joke.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:43.110
I would much rather a future in which vehicles
are sort of on demand and driverless so that

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.110
listen.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:51.790
For most of us, our cars sit in a driveway
on the street or in a garage 90% of the time

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.810
or more of the day.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:13:00.860
Most people most people aren't driving two
and a half hours a day, which is like 10%

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:01.860
of the day.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:06.710
So my preference would be dramatically reduce
the number of vehicles, have an on demand

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:11.870
system where when you actually need a vehicle,
it shows up, gets you where you need to go

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.680
and then brings other people around.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.630
The reforms we need are dramatic, dramatic
and yes, obviously just public transit is

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:19.630
great.

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:24.190
The reality in the United States, when there
are so many suburban and rural areas is it

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:31.220
seems more likely to me that on demand, autonomous
electric vehicles are going to be.

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:36.610
A better fit for parts of the country than
like bus high capacity busses where you just

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:43.140
don't have the number of people needing these
particular routes to justify it financially

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.250
in much of the country.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:45.250
That is the perfect solution.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.519
So listen, I'm with Paul.

00:13:47.519 --> 00:13:51.730
But when it comes to electric vehicles versus
internal combustion engines, I am on the side

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:53.550
of electric vehicles.

